{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":55,"description":"The server-side Stack options object has NO live_preview configuration. The prescribed minimal fix requires adding live_preview: { enable: !!(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN), host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST, management_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN || '' } to the options before Stack creation. Without this, the Contentstack SDK will never subscribe to the preview delivery stream, so SSR/SSG pages never receive preview content. Every acceptance criterion depends on this SDK-level configuration.","suggestedFix":"Add CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST to the process.env destructuring (lines 10-16), then add live_preview to the options object: live_preview: { enable: !!(CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN), host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST || CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST, management_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN || '' }"},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":95,"description":"No includeDraft flag exists on IContentstackGetEntry, IContentstackGetSingleEntry, IContentstackGetSingletonEntry, ICreateQueryConfig, or ICreateEntryConfig. The public-facing functions (getEntry, getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry, findSingletonEntry) do not accept or propagate includeDraft, and none call Stack.livePreviewQuery(previewParams) before .find(). Draft content can never be fetched server-side — the preview site will only show published content.","suggestedFix":"Add includeDraft?: boolean and previewParams?: { live_preview: string; content_type_uid: string } to the relevant interfaces. In getEntry/getSingleEntry/getSingletonEntry, when includeDraft is true, call Stack.livePreviewQuery(previewParams) before .find()/.fetch()/.findOne()."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx","line":62,"description":"The Page component destructures only { content, contentTypeUid } from IPageProps and never passes previewConfig to ContentstackProvider. previewConfig is computed in getStaticProps and included in props, but is never consumed by the page component or threaded into the provider. ContentstackProvider always receives previewConfig as undefined, so isPreviewEnabled is always false and live preview never activates.","suggestedFix":"Destructure previewConfig from IPageProps in the Page component and pass it to ContentstackProvider (or ensure the Layout wrapper passes it through)."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx","line":120,"description":"context.preview is read and used to compute previewConfig, but it is never propagated through to contentstack service calls (getEntry, getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry). The prescribed fix states preview flag must be propagated from getStaticProps context through to factory methods. Without this, activating preview mode cannot trigger draft content fetching server-side.","suggestedFix":"Pass includeDraft: true and previewParams (parsed from context.preview or context.query) to all contentstack service calls in getStaticProps."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx","line":124,"description":"Uses process.env.CONTENTSTACK_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN instead of CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN as prescribed in the root cause analysis. The env var name does not match the prescribed pattern.","suggestedFix":"Use process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_MANAGEMENT_TOKEN and process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":95,"description":"fetchLivePreviewContent creates a new contentstack.Stack() instance on every invocation (every hashchange event). This is wasteful and may cause connection leaks. The prescribed fix states the provider should use the existing server-side Stack, not construct a new SDK client on each fetch.","suggestedFix":"Reuse the existing Stack from src/services/contentstack.ts or accept a contentstack client via props. Do not instantiate a new Stack inside the callback."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":113,"description":"The live preview fetch only updates the 'page' field of IContentstackContent. When a CMS edit changes header, footer, serviceAlerts, staticUpdates, globalDictionary, or any other content type, the preview will not reflect those changes. setLiveContent only merges page entries, failing the acceptance criterion for displaying updated values across all content types.","suggestedFix":"Fetch and merge all relevant content types in fetchLivePreviewContent, or use the SDK's livePreview callback which provides the full updated entry object."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":130","description":"The implementation relies on window 'hashchange' events for real-time updates instead of registering the Contentstack SDK's built-in livePreview callback (Stack.livePreview.onContentUpdate or equivalent). The prescribed fix states the livePreview callback registered via Stack.livePreview should call setContent. Contentstack's Live Preview SDK uses postMessage/WebSocket for real-time updates, not URL hash changes. Relying solely on hashchange may miss updates that don't change the hash.","suggestedFix":"Register Stack.livePreview.onContentUpdate (or @contentstack/live-preview-utils onEntryUpdate) in a useEffect to call setLiveContent with the updated content object. Keep hashchange as a fallback if desired, but the SDK callback is the primary mechanism."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests were added for the live preview / includeDraft functionality. Grep across test/unit/ for 'live_preview', 'livePreview', 'includeDraft', 'include_draft', 'ContentstackContext', 'ContentstackProvider' returned zero matches. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests in test/unit/ mirroring the src/ path. There are no tests verifying that includeDraft: true causes the correct SDK calls, that setContent updates the context and triggers re-renders, that the initial state matches defaultContent, or that hashchange triggers a refetch.","suggestedFix":"Add test/unit/context/ContentstackContext.test.tsx and test/unit/services/contentstack.test.ts covering: includeDraft flag propagation, livePreviewQuery calls, setContent behavior, initial state, and hashchange-triggered refetch."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":100,"description":"The catch block uses console.error instead of the project's logger service. The rest of the codebase uses logger from services/logger. This is inconsistent and may miss structured logging/monitoring.","suggestedFix":"Import logger from services/logger and use logger.error instead of console.error."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":48,"description":"getLivePreviewParams has an empty catch block that silently swallows errors. This makes debugging preview issues difficult. While parsing errors are non-fatal, they should at least be logged.","suggestedFix":"Add a logger.warn or logger.debug call in the catch block to aid debugging."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":85,"description":"The fetchLivePreviewContent callback has a dependency on defaultContent which is an object passed as a prop. Since defaultContent is likely a new reference on every render, this could cause unnecessary re-renders and re-fetching. Consider memoizing defaultContent or using a ref.","suggestedFix":"Use a ref to hold defaultContent or wrap it in useMemo at the call site to stabilize the reference."}],"summary":"The implementation does not satisfy the prescribed minimal fix or the acceptance criteria. The server-side Stack (src/services/contentstack.ts) — the critical root cause — still lacks live_preview configuration entirely. No includeDraft flag is propagated through any public-facing service function. The Page component never passes previewConfig to ContentstackProvider. The client-side provider creates a new Stack on every hashchange, only updates the 'page' content type, and relies on hashchange events instead of the SDK's built-in livePreview callback. Zero vitest unit tests were added. Every acceptance criterion related to displaying draft content, real-time edits, and server-rendered preview is unmet. The verdict is changes_requested with 10 blocker-level issues."}
